                        "review": "Most people have only found this game after the fact, I was sadly around during it's development. The developer was a fool who kept focusing on adding more planes instead of focusing on the content like the story or fixing up bugs. The developer ended up doing this so much that the publisher got tired of waiting and demanded a full release. Additionally the developer made incredibly questionable decisions, for a time this game even had half maneuverability missiles because the developer thought it might be 'too easy'. \n\nTHe developer themself even admits that during the project they entirely lost sight of the end goal and just got focused on working with the community to make 'more'. \n\nI do not truly fault the developer, a passion project can quickly spin out of control but this was too much, too fast, too unskilled (developer's own implication) to handle what was before him with tools that weren't up to snuff. \n\nThis had potential but the only thing that'll save it is what the developer wishes to do, redo VT entirely.",
